    {
      "page_title": "OIDC: id_token vs access_token",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What OIDC Adds",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What turns OAuth into a login?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Add ==scope=openid== to `/authorize` — AS returns an `id_token`",
            "`id_token` = **always** a JWT, for the __client__ to consume: who logged in",
            "`access_token` = for the __API__, may be opaque; client never parses it",
            "Discovery at `/.well-known/openid-configuration`: endpoints, algs, scopes"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "GET /authorize?",
            "  scope=openid profile email",
            "  &nonce=n-8Kx2q9  # client random"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The key idea",
          "text": "id_token answers **who**. access_token answers **what may they do**. Different audience, different reader, never swap them."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Claims Inside an id_token",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Which claims must the client check?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`iss` exact issuer, `aud` = ==this client_id==, `exp`/`iat` fresh",
            "`nonce` must equal the one **you** generated this login",
            "`auth_time` when the user really authenticated; `acr`/`amr` how (mfa, pwd)",
            "`sub` = the only stable user key the issuer promises"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "{ \"iss\":\"https://as.io\",",
            "  \"sub\":\"7f3a-91\", \"aud\":\"spa-01\",",
            "  \"nonce\":\"n-8Kx2q9\",  // must match",
            "  \"amr\":[\"pwd\",\"otp\"] }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Nonce Round Trip",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "client mints nonce",
                "sub": "stores in session"
              },
              {
                "text": "sent on /authorize",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "AS copies into id_token",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "client compares",
                "sub": "mismatch = reject",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blocks ==token injection==: a stolen id_token carries someone else's nonce",
            "`state` guards the redirect; `nonce` guards the __token itself__",
            "One nonce per login attempt, deleted after use"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky-pink",
          "title": "Primary key rule",
          "text": "Store `iss` + `sub` as the user key. Email is a __display attribute__, never an identity."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "cognito",
      "subtitle": "The identity layer"
    },
