        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Profile Claims: /userinfo",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why not put everything in the id_token?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Big or volatile claims (picture, groups, address) bloat every request",
            "`/userinfo` = bearer call with the ==access_token==, returns fresh JSON",
            "Keeps the id_token small and cacheable; fetch profile on demand"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "GET /userinfo",
            "Authorization: Bearer <access_token>",
            "-> {\"sub\":\"7f3a-91\",",
            "    \"email_verified\":true}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sending an id_token to your API as `Bearer` — **wrong aud**, wrong purpose",
            "API accepting an id_token: any client's login token now opens your API",
            "Keying users on `email` — issuers let email change, and reuse it",
            "Trusting `email` when `email_verified` is `false` or absent",
            "Skipping `nonce` compare because 'the signature was valid'"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
