    {
      "page_title": "Refresh, Rotation, Reuse Detection",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why Refresh Exists",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why not one long access token?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Access token stays ==5-15 min==: a stolen copy dies fast",
            "**Refresh** token lives days-months, buys new access tokens",
            "User is not re-prompted; the session feels continuous",
            "Refresh only on the __back channel__ `POST /token`, with client auth",
            "Long life = the {red:crown jewels}: never in JS, never in a URL"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "access_token  exp = 600s",
            "refresh_token exp = 30d",
            "grant_type=refresh_token"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Rotation Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What does rotation actually change?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Every refresh call returns a ==NEW== refresh token",
            "The presented one is invalidated: {red:one-time use}",
            "Tokens form a __family__ chained by a shared `family_id`",
            "Reuse of a spent token = one copy was **stolen**",
            "Response to theft: revoke the {red:whole family}, not one token"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Expiry: Sliding vs Absolute",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Clock",
            "Behaviour",
            "Typical"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Sliding",
              "extends on each use",
              "30 d idle"
            ],
            [
              "Absolute",
              "hard session cap",
              "90 d max"
            ],
            [
              "Both",
              "usual production choice",
              "idle + cap"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{ \"access_token\":\"eyJ...\",",
            "  \"expires_in\": 600,",
            "  \"refresh_token\":\"v1.MRT.bbb\",",
            "  \"token_type\":\"Bearer\" }"
          ],
          "note": "bbb is the ROTATED token — store it"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key idea",
          "text": "The old ==v1.MRT.aaa== is dead the instant {green:bbb} is issued. If aaa ever shows up again, the {red:family dies}."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Defaults",
          "text": "Rotate always, detect reuse, revoke the family, single-flight the client, keep it in an {green:HttpOnly cookie} or behind a BFF."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "iam",
      "subtitle": "Keeping long-lived keys"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "DPoP, the Refresh Race & Why JWTs Resist Revocation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Sender-Constrained Tokens",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do you stop bearer theft entirely?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "**DPoP** (RFC 9449): client signs a proof JWT per request",
            "Header `DPoP:` carries it; token is bound to the public key __jkt__",
            "**mTLS**-bound: token tied to the TLS client certificate",
            "Either way the token stops being a {red:bearer} token — a stolen copy is useless"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "DPoP: eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1Ni...",
            "Authorization: DPoP eyJ..."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. The Concurrency Hazard",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why did rotation log everyone out?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Two parallel calls hit 401 and **both** refresh at once",
            "Second one presents an already-spent token = reuse error",
            "Family revoked, user thrown out — a {red:self-inflicted} logout",
            "Fix: __single-flight__ mutex, one in-flight refresh per app",
            "Multi-tab: elect a {blue:leader tab}, others await via BroadcastChannel",
            "Server side: small ==grace window== (5-10 s) accepting the prior token"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Refresh token issued to a `client_credentials` client — no user, just re-auth",
            "Refresh token handed to browser JS: one **XSS** and the session is permanent",
            "No rotation: a leaked refresh token is valid for months, undetected",
            "Reuse detection revoking only that token, not the {red:family}",
            "Sliding expiry with no absolute cap — a session that never ends"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Core Problem",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why can't you 'log out everywhere' with a plain JWT?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "A signed JWT is valid until ==`exp`== — **nothing** checks a store",
            "Fire a user at 10:00, their 15-min token still works at 10:14",
            "There is no built-in kill switch: the signature already said yes",
            "Revocation = re-introducing state you removed on purpose"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "# fired at 10:00:00",
            "exp = 1767225300  # 10:15:00",
            "# API verifies sig + exp = 200 OK",
            "# for 15 more minutes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Summary",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Stateless speed vs immediate revocation is a ==dial, not a binary==. Turn it with the access-token TTL.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
