    {
      "page_title": "Revocation: /revoke, Introspection & Denylists",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: What You Can Kill",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What does `POST /revoke` (RFC 7009) actually kill?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Send `token` + `token_type_hint` to the AS with client auth",
            "Kills the ==refresh token== (and its family) __immediately__",
            "Already-issued **access tokens keep working** until `exp`",
            "Always returns `200` even for unknown tokens — no oracle"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /revoke",
            "token=8xLOxBtZp8&",
            "token_type_hint=refresh_token",
            "-> 200 OK (always)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How does introspection (RFC 7662) give an exact answer?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Resource server POSTs the token to `/introspect`, gets `active`",
            "Truth is **live** — the AS owns the state, latency is ~zero",
            "Costs one ==network hop per request== on the hot path",
            "Cache the `active:true` result for {orange:5-30s}, not minutes"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /introspect  token=...",
            "{\"active\":true,",
            " \"sub\":\"u_91\",\"exp\":...}",
            "# active:false = stop now"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Denylist and Epoch",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do you denylist a JWT without an unbounded list?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Key by ==`jti`== for one token, or `sub` + `iat` cutoff for all of a user's",
            "Set the Redis TTL to the token's own **`exp`** — dead entries self-delete",
            "List size is bounded by revocations in one access-token lifetime",
            "Verification adds one `GET` — ~0.2ms local, still stateful"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "SET revoked:jti:9f2a 1 EXAT 1767225300",
            "SET epoch:u_91 1767225000",
            "# verify: iat < epoch -> 401"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The epoch bump",
          "text": "==Password change==, role downgrade, MFA reset and account deletion must all bump `epoch:<sub>`. Verification rejects any token with `iat` **<** the epoch — one write revokes every token that user holds."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule",
          "text": "Revocation you never tested is revocation you do not have. Fire a test user and time how long their token keeps working — that number, not your policy doc, is your exposure window."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "redis",
      "subtitle": "Killing live tokens"
    },
