        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Q: localStorage or cookie?",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Where does a browser hold an access token?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==localStorage/sessionStorage==: any JS on origin reads it — one **XSS** exfiltrates every token",
            "But no ==automatic CSRF== risk: you attach it by hand",
            "==HttpOnly+Secure+SameSite cookie==: invisible to JS, sent **automatically**",
            "Auto-send means ==CSRF defence is mandatory=="
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "localStorage.getItem('tok') // XSS wins",
            "Set-Cookie: sid=..; HttpOnly;",
            "  Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/"
          ]
